    "The Local Planning Authority, having regard to its own records and the evidence submitted by the applicant, considers that, on the balance of probability, the property known as 35A Croyland Road, London, N9 7BB has been used and occupied as a self-contained one-bedroom flat continuously for a period exceeding four years prior to the date of the application. Accordingly, the use is considered lawful and, in accordance with Section 191 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 (as amended), a Certificate of Lawfulness for the existing use of the property as a self-contained residential flat can be granted."
